"""Real geometry for the doorway cart on the 1764029361010 clip.

Every number here was read out of that run's own tracking JSON
(1764029361010_B8A44F67FC21-medium_tracking.json), so it is what the pipeline
actually saw. 1280x720, 20 fps, 425 frames, camera placement
"Outside (facing entrance)". The slice is frames 1-100.

WHAT THE CLIP SHOWS
-------------------
C1 is a loaded, unbagged cart standing in the doorway from the first frame. P2
walks up to it, stands at it, and walks off inward; nobody else ever touches it.
The cart stays in the doorway, resolves OUTBOUND, and the run should call it a
PUSHOUT ALERT on the abandonment route once P2 is gone.

The contact is not in doubt: P2's overlap with the cart climbs to 0.3139 on frame
32 and holds at or above 0.2 for frames 21-33. But the link is not made on first
contact. Other people are in frame and overlapping too, so this is a CONTESTED
cart and confirmation takes LINK_CONTESTED_FRAMES, not LINK_CONFIRM_FRAMES: the
link lands on frame 35, by which time P2 is already stepping away and the overlap
has fallen to 0.1388.

That is why the other two people are in this fixture even though neither ever
owns the cart. Replay P2 alone and the cart is uncontested, the link confirms on
frame 21 at 0.2271, and the defect below cannot be reproduced at all.

WHY THAT MATTERED
-----------------
`_link_peak_iou` used to be seeded with the FORMATION FRAME's IoU and grow only
from there. The formation frame was 0.1388, every later frame was lower, so the
parked-cart release read 0.1388 against LINK_OWNED_PEAK_IOU (0.15), called the
link never-real, and reported the cart DISOWNED on frame 90. Disownment makes the
tracker forget the remembered owner, and a cart with no owner can never be
`abandoned` - so `abandoned` was False for all 425 frames and the run finalised
`partial|unbagged OUTBOUND score=55` MEDIUM PRIORITY instead of 75 PUSHOUT ALERT.

The formation frame is the wrong place to measure a relationship whose evidence
sits a confirmation delay behind it. Seeding the peak from the candidacy as well
reads 0.3139 and the cart keeps its owner.

The 1764200318790 shopper the disown branch was written for is still caught by
the same number: peak IoU 0.064 over six frames, candidacy included. See
LINK_OWNED_PEAK_IOU and tests/fixtures/parked_cart_geometry.py.

The cart is genuinely parked throughout - its centroid extent measures 11.2 px
against LINK_STATIC_SPREAD_PX (12.0) - so `_link_moved_under`, the other half of
the possession test, is False here. Peak IoU is the only thing standing between
this cart and a false disown, which is why it is what gets pinned.

Boxes are (x1, y1, x2, y2) and centroids (cx, cy), exactly as the linker receives
them.
"""

